                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "962dde9f-43cf-36ab-975e-a9ca51c8fad5",
                        "entry_id": "06303f6f-6787-3717-9aaf-e1d48b3b9ba3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Before; in advance of the time of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "58f6c63c-a718-4ad1-ad44-40d8229e7fb2",
                                "sense_id": "962dde9f-43cf-36ab-975e-a9ca51c8fad5",
                                "text": "He said he was jealous, and craved something to ease his care. 'It's but a small thing I ask,' says he, 'but it will make me a happy man, and nothing ever shall come atween us. Tryst wi' me for Beltane's E'en on the Sker sands, at the green link o' the burn where the sands begin, on the ebb o' the tide when midnight is by, but afore cockcrow. For,' said he, 'that was our forbears' tryst for true lovers, and wherefore no for you and me?'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71c7bcfe-388c-48d4-8c91-1bc96f1d370f",
                                "sense_id": "962dde9f-43cf-36ab-975e-a9ca51c8fad5",
                                "text": "\"Oh aye!\" his face lit up with a smile. \"I mind that! Where was that?\" \"That was us when we all worked in the shop, afore the War.\" \"Oh aye …?\" he frowned. \"Who …?\" She took the photograph back from him and reached inside her apron pocket for her spectacles."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
